
### 📋 Veridian OS Notification API Guide
 * 📂 **Setup & Initialization**
   * 📜 **Loadstring Execution**
     * 💡 *Copy and run this code to import the library:*
     ```lua
     local NeonNotify = loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modcreate1641-collab/VeridianProject/refs/heads/main/Notification-OS-library.lua"))()
     
     ```
 * 📂 **API Methods**
   * 🛠️ **NeonNotify:Notify(config)** — *Sends a queued neon notification to the screen.*
     * ⚙️ Style (String) — *OS Theme selection:* "Samsung", "Apple", "Vivo", "Xiaomi", "Windows", "macOS" *(Default: "Apple")*
     * ⚙️ Title (String) — *Header text of the notification.* *(Default: "System")*
     * ⚙️ Content (String) — *Main description/message body.*
     * ⚙️ Duration (Number) — *Display time in seconds before dismiss.* *(Default: 3.5)*
   * 🛠️ **NeonNotify:SetStyle(styleName)** — *Changes the global default theme for future notifications.*
     * ⚙️ styleName (String) — *Accepts any of the 6 OS choices listed above.*
 * 📂 **Usage Examples**
   * 🚀 **Full Configuration Syntax**
     ```lua
     NeonNotify:Notify({
         Style = "Samsung",
         Title = "Exploit Loaded",
         Content = "Script is fully active and running in queue.",
         Duration = 5
     })
     
     ```
   * ⚠️ **Minimalist Syntax (Fallback Safeguard)**
     ```lua
     -- Missing Title/Style will auto-fallback to "System" and default theme without errors
     NeonNotify:Notify({
         Content = "Quick system status update."
     })
     
     ```
   * 🌐 **Changing Global OS Theme**
     ```lua
     NeonNotify:SetStyle("Windows")
     
     ```
